    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0993" n="931" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg931"/>

                <head>No. 532.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Heap.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1878-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 136.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 259, of the 25th ultimo, describing a visit which you made in
                    December last, on the United States steamer Gettysburg, to various ports on the
                    Tunisian coast, during which you state that the officers and crew of the
                    Gettysburg, as well as yourself, were very hospitably received.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to inform the Bey of Tunis that the President appreciates the
                    attentions which were shown to the officers and crew of the Gettysburg.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp; c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
